Okay, furthest I've ever gotten in Nethack. A barbarian named
Clockwork, xp level 17, 174 max hp, -22 AC fully equipped. Fire, cold
and sleep resistances had been picked up. Telepathy, stealth, extra
luck from throwing a few gems to a convenient gray unicorn. I found
several wishes earlier and got GDSM, speed boots, gauntlets of power. I
also found a magic marker (99 charges, blessed it and wrote out geno
scrolls with it) and the artifact Cleaver.

Anyhow, I had just went back down to the Medusa level (legend template)
after trekking up to find a blindfold. Going to the right side of the
level, what do I find? An archon! While navigating the section it casts
a spell that makes monsters aware of my presence over and over again.
At one point 4 storm giants appear, and I kill them and eat one for
shock resistance. Yes! Anyway, moving onto the center room with Medusa
in it, I kick the door open. The archon approaches me...and casts
create monster. I'm surrounded by a dragon, a xorn, various other
beasties...but it isn't done yet. While I fend them off the archon
casts it again, and again, and AGAIN, creating master mind flayers and
minotaurs and trolls and giants and green slimes. I'm surrounded by
monsters and they come faster then I can kill them. I'm forced to use
my prayer to remove some sliming as I didn't have a source of fire
handy. Surrounded by seemingly endless beasts I (rather stupidly) pull
a scroll of teleportation out and try to read it. Duh, me, the medusa
level is teleport-proofed. My last move?

"You smite it. You are splashed! You die..."

1570 creatures vanquished, DL 27 reached, 751280 points. Killed by an
ochre jelly after 46460 moves.



